{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>I will drive out nations from before you.</b> The verse is precise in saying <b>from before you</b> — meaning, so that you not suffer distress at the sight of them, after the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Gittin 56b) in the episode of Rabbi Yochanan ben Zakkai with Aspasianus: HaShem promised that they will not appear before us at all, fundamentally." "<b>And I will broaden, etc.</b> After the manner of what Scripture says (Jeremiah 3:19) ״אֶרֶץ צְבִי״, and our Sages of blessed memory said (Gittin 57b): like the skin of a tzvi, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:35.240420068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}